  "youtube": {
    "title": "Ignoring Your Phone Isn't Enough #shorts",
    "description": "You hear the buzz, you don't check it, you keep working. Focus saved? Not quite.\n\nIn a study with 166 students doing an attention task, those who simply received a call or text notification (without touching their phone) made more mistakes. The hit to focus was almost as big as actually using the phone.\n\nWhen it matters: Do Not Disturb on, notifications off, then work.\n\nResearch: Stothart, Mitchum & Yehnert (2015), \"The Attentional Cost of Receiving a Cell Phone Notification\", Journal of Experimental Psychology: Human Perception and Performance.\n\n#shorts #focus #productivity #psychology #studytips #animation #selfimprovement",
